## Recognising a mode on screen

Nothing in the app needs the Core to know the mode: a gun's own Smart Actions (set in
All guns) run on the gun alone, in every mode. A mode's page and its pairs need the Core
to recognise the mode as it recognises a gun, from a taught picture of a part of the
screen that (a) only that mode shows and (b) stays on screen for the whole match, because
the Core runs an area's actions only while its picture stands (D110, D119). A lobby
banner is no use: it is gone once the match starts. What the research found:

- **Build or Zero Build** is the easiest: Build matches show the wood, stone and metal
  counters; Zero Build shows a Pocket Item slot where the build button was (Epic: "Pocket
  Items have replaced the old Build button"). Teach the counters' corner of the HUD once in
  each mode.
- **Reload** on any map: while a teammate is alive, being eliminated shows a reboot
  countdown instead of the spectate screen (not on screen all match, so a helper cue only);
  each Reload map is its own island on the minimap (Springfield's Simpsons POI names,
  Oasis, Mini-Venture's five POIs).
- **Fortnite OG**: the minimap shows the Chapter 1 island (Loot Lake, Dusty Depot...).
- **Blitz Royale**: the players-left counter starts near 32, not 100, and the Blitz Level
  shows; always Zero Build.
- **Arenas Boxfights**: a round score racing to the win limit, fights in small boxes.
- **Respawn Rumble**: a team score counting to 40 instead of a players-left counter.
- **Ranked** could not be told from unranked from any Epic source: Epic documents the rank
  emblem only in the lobby and after the match. A cup match looks like a Ranked one.

None of this is tested on real frames yet. The most reliable first try is the minimap
corner (it names the island) together with the build counters' corner.

