**How the history was assembled.** The backbone is the community Fortnite Wiki's weapon
category pages (Assault Weapons, Submachine Guns, Shotguns, Pistols, Sniper Rifles,
Marksman Rifles, Bows, Crossbows, Explosive Weapons, Melee Weapons, Ranged Weapons), read
through its API, chapter by chapter. Each chapter was then checked, season by season,
against the wiki's loot-pool pages (which added what the category pages miss, such as the
Infinity Blade) and against Epic's own pages: the patch notes and news on epicgames.com and
fortnite.com (read through the Wayback Machine, which is cited as the Epic URL), the update
notes on communities.epicgames.com, and the Creative release notes on dev.epicgames.com.
447 of the 521 guns are named on at least one Epic page, cited in their `sources`; the other 74 are named only by the community wiki and each says
so in its `uncertain` sentence (listed below).

