(Chapter 7's research re-listed the returning guns it found in its pools, so the rows add
up to more than the list; the list has one entry per name.)

**One entry per name the game shows.** Rarity versions (Common to Legendary) are one
entry, and so are the Mythic "Enhanced X" versions and the higher-tier models of X. A named
Mythic ("Skye's Assault Rifle") and every Exotic, Lawless, Unstable, Eradicator, Heisted,
Lawful or Morphite weapon whose name differs is its own entry. A name that came back in a
later chapter is the same entry, dated from its first appearance (`from`). Folded into
another entry because it is the same weapon: Luke's Green Lightsaber, Machine Pistol.

**What counts as a gun.** Every weapon a player can pick up and use in an Epic-made
mode: assault rifles (with LMGs, miniguns and blasters), SMGs, shotguns, pistols,
sniper and marksman rifles, bows, crossbows, explosives (launchers and the thrown
explosives the wiki counts as weapons), melee weapons, and **Items**: the weapon-like
hotbar items that deal damage with the fire button (Harpoon Gun, Mythic Goldfish, the
Marvel and anime powers, Rocket Ram, Sonic Power Sneakers...). Not healing, shields,
food, movement-only items, vehicles, traps, Save the World, Creative-only weapons, or a
weapon only a boss holds. Where one chapter's research counted a borderline item as a
weapon because it deals damage (Wings of Icarus, War Machine's Auto Turret, Blizzard
Grenade), it is in the list.

**Classes are ours** (Fortnite has no class tabs); they follow Epic's Creative weapon
subcategories ([Fortnite Weapons Primer](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/fortnite/fortnite-weapons-primer))
and each research pass's reading of Epic's own description ("Assault Weapon: ..."). Every
drum gun is with the SMGs, where the Drum Gun's own id has been since the first version
of this list, though Chapter 1 called it an Assault Weapon. Inside a class the guns in a
