An id is never given to anything else. When a gun leaves every mode's pool it stays in the
list with `usedBy: []` (it is vaulted, not gone), so an id retires only if a weapon is
taken out of the list altogether; give a returning one its old id back from this table.

| id | name | left the list | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| (none) | | | every id of the first version is still here; the `zero_build` group was dissolved, not its id |

## How to refresh this list (every update, and every new season)

Fortnite changes its pools at every season and at every update inside one (v42.10, v42.20,
...: about every two weeks), and Arenas about weekly. On each one:

1. **Find Epic's notes.** On communities.epicgames.com, per mode: Battle Royale
   (https://communities.epicgames.com/channel/wvDV/battle-royale), Reload, Fortnite OG, Blitz
   and Arenas (https://communities.epicgames.com/channel/mjGG/arenas) each post "vNN.NN ...
   Update Notes". communities.epicgames.com answers a plain script (`curl`); fortnite.com and
   epicgames.com refuse scripts, so read those in a browser or through the Wayback Machine.
2. **Update each mode's `loadout.pool`.** Battle Royale and Arenas: Epic lists what is new,
   unvaulted, vaulted and (Battle Royale) the new Loot Hacks. Reload, OG and Blitz: Epic lists
   only changes; apply them to the pool here, and cross-check with the wiki's
   `Template:Reload_Loot_Pool`, `Template:Blitz_Loot_Pool` and the OG season's `Loot_Pool` page.
   A gun leaving a pool stays in the list; take the mode out of its `usedBy`. A mode that
   ends stays out of the list (say so under "Not in the list as modes"); a new mode with a
   pool gets an entry in its family, id = family + "." + slug of its name.
3. **Keep `usedBy` and every pool agreeing** (the test checks both directions).
4. **A new gun:** add it to its class, id = class + "." + slug of its name (`../README.md`),
   `from` = the season as Epic names it, `sources` = the notes page, `uncertain` = `null`
   unless something is not certain. Check the whole list for the name first: a returning
   gun already has an entry and keeps its id.
5. **Pictures.** Epic's own only, from the notes' images
   (`https://fn-creator-community-cdn.qstv.on.epicgames.com/<uuid>/post-image-block_2048x1152.webp`)
   or fortnite.com news (`cms-assets.unrealengine.com/...`, older `cdn2.unrealengine.com/...`).
   Crop to the weapon, `im.thumbnail((480, 300))`, save as `weapons/<slug>.png` (a mode's key
   art as `modes/<slug>.png`), and add a row to the Pictures table.
6. Set `asOf` and `season`, run `node dashboard/tools/test-game-data.js` and
   `node dashboard/tools/test-auto-modes.js`, then rebuild the exe and run
   `node dashboard/tools/sync-mobile.js`, which copies this folder into the phone app.
